@baseUrl = http://localhost:5260

# Run top to bottom against a freshly started app (the in-memory database is reset on every start).
# The data seeded at startup is household 1 with user 1. Ids in the comments assume a fresh start.
# Dates assume that today is 2026-11-10 (a Tuesday). Adjust the dates if you run it on another day.
# Enums are numbers. FrequencyType: Daily 0, Weekly 1, Monthly 2, Yearly 3.
# Weekdays are flags: Monday 1, Tuesday 2, Wednesday 4, Thursday 8, Friday 16, Saturday 32, Sunday 64.
# MeasurementUnit: Gram 0, Kilogram 1, Milliliter 2, Deciliter 3, Liter 4, Piece 5, Teaspoon 6, Tablespoon 7, Cup 8.

# Household
### Gets all households, should contain the seeded household 1

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Households

### Gets the household with id 1

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Households/1

### Gets the household with id 999, should return 404

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Households/999

### Adds a new household, gets id 2

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Households
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Aa"
}

### Name with only one character, should return 400

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Households
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "A"
}

### Updates household name for id 2

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Households/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Changed household name"
}

### Update with no changes, should return 200

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Households/2
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Deletes household 2

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/Households/2

### Household 2 is gone, should return 404

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Households/2

