# Chore validation
### Weekly rule without weekdays, should return 400

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/new-chore
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Invalid chore",
  "householdId": 1,
  "frequency": 1,
  "periodStartDate": "2026-11-10T00:00:00+01:00"
}

### Weekdays on a monthly rule, should return 400

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/new-chore
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Invalid chore",
  "householdId": 1,
  "frequency": 2,
  "weekdays": 1,
  "periodStartDate": "2026-11-10T00:00:00+01:00"
}

### Interval of 0, should return 400

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/new-chore
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Invalid chore",
  "householdId": 1,
  "frequency": 0,
  "interval": 0,
  "periodStartDate": "2026-11-10T00:00:00+01:00"
}

### Weekdays without frequency, should return 400

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/new-chore
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Invalid chore",
  "householdId": 1,
  "weekdays": 1,
  "periodStartDate": "2026-11-10T00:00:00+01:00"
}

# Chore and ChoreInstance
### Creates a one-off chore without a rule, gets chore 1 and instance 1

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/new-chore
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mop the floors",
  "householdId": 1,
  "periodStartDate": "2026-11-10T00:00:00+01:00"
}

### Vacuum every Monday and Thursday (9), chore 2. The instance on 12 Nov is created by hand, the rest is generated up to 4 weeks ahead

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/new-chore
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Vacuum",
  "householdId": 1,
  "frequency": 1,
  "weekdays": 9,
  "startDate": "2026-11-09",
  "periodStartDate": "2026-11-12T00:00:00+01:00"
}

### Change the sheets every second Sunday (64), chore 3. Should give 15 Nov and 29 Nov

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/new-chore
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Change the sheets",
  "householdId": 1,
  "frequency": 1,
  "interval": 2,
  "weekdays": 64,
  "startDate": "2026-11-15",
  "periodStartDate": "2026-11-15T00:00:00+01:00"
}

### Pay the rent on the 31st every month, chore 4. November has 30 days, so it falls on 30 Nov

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/new-chore
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Pay the rent",
  "householdId": 1,
  "frequency": 2,
  "startDate": "2026-10-31",
  "periodStartDate": "2026-11-30T00:00:00+01:00"
}

### Gets all chores for household 1

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores?householdId=1

### Gets chore 2

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores/2

### Gets chore 999, should return 404

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores/999

### Gets all instances for household 1

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances?householdId=1

### Gets the instances for the week 9 Nov to 16 Nov (to is not included). Note that + in the time zone must be written as %2B

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances?householdId=1&from=2026-11-09T00:00:00%2B01:00&to=2026-11-16T00:00:00%2B01:00

### Gets instance 2

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/2

### Instance for a chore that doesn't exist, should return 404

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "choreId": 999,
  "periodStartDate": "2026-11-10T00:00:00+01:00"
}

### Creates an extra instance for chore 1

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "choreId": 1,
  "periodStartDate": "2026-11-11T00:00:00+01:00"
}

### Marks instance 1 as done

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/1/mark-as-done

### Clears the done date on instance 1

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/1/clear-done-date

### Skips instance 3 (Vacuum on 16 Nov). It stays in the list with isSkipped true and is not generated again

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/3/mark-as-skipped

### Skips instance 4 and then clears it again

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/4/mark-as-skipped

###

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/4/clear-skipped-date

### Marks the skipped instance 3 as done, which clears the skip

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/3/mark-as-done

### Skips instance 3 again, which clears the done date

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/3/mark-as-skipped

### Updates the name on chore 4

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores/4
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Pay the rent on time"
}

### Assigns chore 2 to user 1

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 1
}

### Only the chores for user 1, should be chore 2

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores?householdId=1&userId=1

### Only the instances for user 1, should be the instances for chore 2

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances?householdId=1&userId=1

### Adds a rule to chore 1 without startDate, should return 400

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "frequency": 0
}

### Chore 3 becomes weekly on Sundays (64) every week. Open instances from today are generated again after the new rule

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores/3
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "frequency": 1,
  "interval": 1,
  "weekdays": 64,
  "startDate": "2026-11-15"
}

### Instances for chore 3 are now every Sunday, should be 15, 22 and 29 Nov and 6 Dec

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances?householdId=1&from=2026-11-14T00:00:00%2B01:00&to=2026-12-08T00:00:00%2B01:00

### Weekdays on a daily rule, should return 400

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores/3
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "frequency": 0,
  "weekdays": 1
}

### Renames chore 2 for the future, should return a NEW chore 5 with a new id and the same rule. Open instances from tomorrow move over to it, the skipped one stays on chore 2

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores/2/update-future
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Vacuum everything"
}

### Chore 2 has only the skipped instance left, chore 5 has the rest and does not get 16 Nov

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances?householdId=1&from=2026-11-09T00:00:00%2B01:00&to=2026-12-08T00:00:00%2B01:00

### Nothing changed, should return chore 5 itself (same id, no new chore created)

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores/5/update-future
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Vacuum everything"
}

### Chore without a rule (chore 1), should return 404

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores/1/update-future
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Whatever"
}

### Deletes one instance of the recurring chore 5. The chore stays. It is created again by the nightly generation, so skipping is the right way to leave one out

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/18

### Deletes both instances of the one-off chore 1, the chore is removed with the last one

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/1

###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/13

### Chore 1 is gone, should return 404

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores/1

# Images
### Uploads an image for recipe 1

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Recipes/1/image
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----HouseholdBoundary

------HouseholdBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./HttpSamples/sample.png
------HouseholdBoundary--

### Gets the image for recipe 1, should return image/png

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Recipes/1/image

### Recipe 1 should now have hasImage true

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Recipes/1

### A text file named .png, should return 400 because the content is checked

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Recipes/1/image
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----HouseholdBoundary

------HouseholdBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="not-an-image.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./HttpSamples/not-an-image.png
------HouseholdBoundary--

### A PDF as recipe image, should return 400

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Recipes/1/image
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----HouseholdBoundary

------HouseholdBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./HttpSamples/sample.pdf
------HouseholdBoundary--

### Image for a recipe that doesn't exist, should return 404

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Recipes/999/image
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----HouseholdBoundary

------HouseholdBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./HttpSamples/sample.png
------HouseholdBoundary--

### Removes the image from recipe 1

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/Recipes/1/image

### The image is gone, should return 404

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Recipes/1/image

# SchoolPlan
### Uploads a school plan for the week of 9 Nov (any date in the week is moved to the Monday), gets id 1

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/SchoolPlans
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----HouseholdBoundary

------HouseholdBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="householdId"

1
------HouseholdBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="weekDate"

2026-11-12
------HouseholdBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./HttpSamples/sample.pdf
------HouseholdBoundary--

